{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513813-dark-thaumaturgy-is-actually-pretty-cool","id":1513813,"title":"Dark Thaumaturgy is actually pretty cool","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-03T14:13:59-07:00","id":1513813,"title":"Dark Thaumaturgy is actually pretty cool","content":"Now I have never actually played as an internalist, but after looking at Dark Thaumaturgy paths for a bit I can kind of see why some would want to be one. A lot of the powers are just really interesting and creative. For example, in Path of Evil Revelations at the lowest level, the internalist can see into the spirit world, but at the highest level, they can create a demon from someone's sins and have it hunt that individual down. Or Tyranny of the Wyrm which can affect true faith, graft bane spirits onto an individual, and even turn someone into demon bait.<br /> <br /> Of course, the mechanics and drawbacks behind the powers limit their effectiveness, but for the most part, they sound pretty amazing.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T14:24:43-07:00","id":1513814,"title":"","content":"Honestly wish they'd just be balanced better so they can enter a normal thaumaturge's repetoir. Fluff says non-infernalists can do all the things infernalists can it's just infernalism is a shortcut, and there's mechanics for learning foreign paths/rituals, yet all too often DT gets paths and rituals that are really powerful with no ethical issues and one really needs to question why everyone isn't learning Aport object or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T14:31:10-07:00","id":1513816,"title":"","content":"Well that's the trick isn't it? They are very good powers. Can't hook a fish without bait. I once played a tremere archon who acquired path of phobos through the capture of infernalists and their grimoires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T15:13:33-07:00","id":1513820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513813-dark-thaumaturgy-is-actually-pretty-cool?p=1513814#post1513814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly wish they'd just be balanced better so they can enter a normal thaumaturge's repetoir. Fluff says non-infernalists can do all the things infernalists can it's just infernalism is a shortcut, and there's mechanics for learning foreign paths/rituals, yet all too often DT gets paths and rituals that are really powerful with no ethical issues and one really needs to question why everyone isn't learning Aport object or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, thats bugged me too. The biggest issue I have though, is that DT seems to allow the infernalist to easily summon and control demons, beings that can be extremely versatile. But a Vampire with Spirit Manipulation is going to have a hard time just conversing with spirits, not because of any language barrier, but because spirits simply dont like vampires. I really dont understand why the writers are making it this hard to interact with the spirit world, and why they are limiting interaction mostly to the low umbra, when the middle umbra is far more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 06-03-2023, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T16:36:57-07:00","id":1513826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513813-dark-thaumaturgy-is-actually-pretty-cool?p=1513814#post1513814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly wish they'd just be balanced better so they can enter a normal thaumaturge's repetoir. Fluff says non-infernalists can do all the things infernalists can it's just infernalism is a shortcut, and there's mechanics for learning foreign paths/rituals, yet all too often DT gets paths and rituals that are really powerful with no ethical issues and one really needs to question why everyone isn't learning Aport object or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc Revised had specific drawbacks to using DT that I don\u2019t remember being a part of V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T04:16:19-07:00","id":1514448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513813-dark-thaumaturgy-is-actually-pretty-cool?p=1513820#post1513820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a Vampire with Spirit Manipulation is going to have a hard time just conversing with spirits, not because of any language barrier, but because spirits simply dont like vampires. I really dont understand why the writers are making it this hard to interact with the spirit world, and why they are limiting interaction mostly to the low umbra, when the middle umbra is far more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was often wandering what is the source , in World of Darkness guides, books and supplements, of the philosophies, methods, notions, and ideas responsible for the rules, and the circumstances, and the attiudes that make it seem - and often might lead to - Kindred ( and also Ghouls and Revenants ) making choices that make them distant and reluctant to deal with and become involved with the Umbra and various Magical Spirits and Supernatural Beings related to these levels, occurences, events, and areas.<br /> <br /> Of course there is the Astral World or the Astral Umbra - a favourite of many Kindred, perhaps especially Vampiresses with Auspex or some type of Blood Magic.<br /> There are also the Shadowlands or the Dark Umbra - a seeminlgy onvious and natural travel, interest, knowledge, and social centre point for Vampires.. This type and category of similar and related levels, rareas, and regions has the good quality of possible positive contact and cooperation with Wraiths.<br /> <br /> What about other types of Umbra, Supernatural Worlds, and Magical Regions ; and the Magical Spirits and Supernatural Beings who dwell in them ? Is it possible to find in some early VtM or Wod books a definite standard and extensive description of the attitude of Vampires towards these areas, regions, occurences, events, beings, and persons ? Certainly the attitude defined and mentioned in many chapters and pragraphs could very well have origin in some distinct and particular descriptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T11:50:43-07:00","id":1514491,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about infernalism to be sure but I'm happy that there's goodies in it. If you can't offer something cool to the player or NPC then its really hard to explain why someone of moderate or more intelligence would become an infernalist. Given experience from other settings in my group many characters can be interesting in becoming evil/&quot;evil&quot; if there's cool stuff for them in it.<br /> <br /> If you can't tempt characters into evil I don't know how demons and such in a setting with a Judeo-Christian mythological inspiration are supposed to work. And you can't really tempt people unless you got something which they would want to have, like really cool and unique Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Or at least that's how I look at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T12:21:59-07:00","id":1514494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513813-dark-thaumaturgy-is-actually-pretty-cool?p=1513820#post1513820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea, thats bugged me too. The biggest issue I have though, is that DT seems to allow the infernalist to easily summon and control demons, beings that can be extremely versatile. But a Vampire with Spirit Manipulation is going to have a hard time just conversing with spirits, not because of any language barrier, but because spirits simply dont like vampires. I really dont understand why the writers are making it this hard to interact with the spirit world, and why they are limiting interaction mostly to the low umbra, when the middle umbra is far more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, for me it's not a really big deal. In most powers where the Thaumaturge can control demons, it's also stated that the consequences can be dire if they fail or do something stupid, the same applies to Spirit Manipulation, the difference being that you can make a fetish with Spirit Manipulation and that's in my opinion much graver than commanding a demon/spirit to do your bidding for a while before sending it back to hell.<br /> <br /> Normally, nobody likes to be enslaved, so it's only natural that they're going to state that &quot;spirits usually don't like vampires&quot;, heck they don't need to like it! They just need to do as I say hahaha...(ofc then there's the flavour text stating that the fetishes could fail at inappropriate times, but that's just to give yet another excuse for the ST to be a dick (as if it was needed lol), as it's basically a ST's job to be a dick some/many times, it's all as expected...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T12:56:35-07:00","id":1514498,"title":"","content":"I look at it that the earlier books that introduced DT (The Sabbat sourcebooks) were quite one dimensional to promote the infernal enemy within concept.<br /> <br /> My head-canon is that any Thaumaturgy or Sorcery can be infernal or Wyrm tainted simply by the caster wishing to power the ritual through unspeakable acts rather than paying for it themselves, demons and banes just won\u2019t respond to summons without unspeakable acts.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are hardly white vampire wizards they are evil and absolutely capable of getting innocents to pay the piper, summoning demons/banes and worse.<br /> <br /> Plus the Tremere don\u2019t have the monopoly on embracing occultists, sorcerors or even Mage, any clan can, look at Mithras orchestrating the Malkavian embrace of Aleicester Crowley, any of these neonates could introduce infernal trappings to Thaumaturgic practice.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve always disliked the broad-brush vampires are unnatural so the entire middle umbra hates them, the KOTE are exiles from heaven who are just as unnatural (more so they dragged themselves out of the Yomi Worlds) and have unfettered access to all realms.<br /> <br /> In addition to kindred with auspex accessing the High Astral Umbras penumbra, I have them equally capable of accessing the Dark Umbra.<br /> <br /> Likewise the middle umbra is vast with numerous dark and malevolent realms and spirits of death, blood and predation any of which would happily interact with kindred (probably more than shifters) even if to elicit Chimage, favours or to further their own designs.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 06-10-2023, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T13:32:28-07:00","id":1514608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513813-dark-thaumaturgy-is-actually-pretty-cool?p=1513814#post1513814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly wish they'd just be balanced better so they can enter a normal thaumaturge's repetoir. Fluff says non-infernalists can do all the things infernalists can it's just infernalism is a shortcut, and there's mechanics for learning foreign paths/rituals, yet all too often DT gets paths and rituals that are really powerful with no ethical issues and one really needs to question why everyone isn't learning Aport object or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lines get even more blurred when you look at how morally bankrupt Vanilla Thaum is. Blood and viscera are common requirements, Sacrificing babies, sewing together live vampires, and chanting to ancient gods is standard practice in many rituals, and the fire and brimstone thing is already baked into the aesthetic of wizards and fireballs. There's no real functional difference, especially considering vampires are already damned to begin with.<br /> <br /> I swear thaumaturges are just infernalists dug so deep into the closet that they broke into Lucifer's wine cellar and started using it in their rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T01:31:55-07:00","id":1514662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513813-dark-thaumaturgy-is-actually-pretty-cool?p=1513816#post1513816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's the trick isn't it? They are very good powers. Can't hook a fish without bait. I once played a tremere archon who acquired path of phobos through the capture of infernalists and their grimoires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in general thaumaturgy was supposed to have flashy and attractive powers that really make others envious and thus it's wielders paranoid. DT being MORE flashy in it's application feels a little wasted, and also like something that only noobs would go for while professional sorcerer types would be quite happy with what they got. Like if you have a relatively safe environment and a path towards mastery of Lure of Flames then Fires of the Inferno seems like an extravagance. Rules wise, FoI is strictly more powerful than LoF and if you were to offer a neonate in a bad spot a choice they'd very probably pick FoI but it's more of a masquerade risk and at 5th level in either path everything should die just the same and you probably shouldn't be over-invested in causing death. Similar arguments could be found in corruption VS defiler. <br /> <br /> Personally, I imagine Tremere have the entire infernal library already converted into vanilla thaumaturgy, they just don't teach it because it'll unnecessarily harm their reputation. <br /> <br /> But then we move onto price. IDK, I'd prefer to see that as something intrinsic to infernalists channeling demonic powers they don't rightfully own (If they used Lure of Flames, it'd have a price, probably smells of sulphur or something) than something you just receive from learning the power. Even then I see it as a temporary punishment for infernalists and their issues go away if they don't use the power for a long time, with higher level powers having longer side effects. The only exception is evil revelations, because putting hellish knowledge into your mind is bound to have consequences no matter how you do it. <br /> <br /> <br /> How then do I make DT more tempting? Well it's cheaper and easier to learn<br /> -DT is always at in-clan costs, and learning paths through DT has them at current rating x3. The character can convert DT path levels to regular path levels by paying the XP difference. <br /> -DT is added to a vampire's thaumaturgy score, so someone with thaumaturgy 2 and DT 2 has a rating of 4. This goes to usual generational limits. While the Path of Blood can raise these limits, it's quite taxing to learn rituals above the 5th level while using this power. <br /> -DT users can add their DT rating to their occult rating for rituals, up to the usual generational limits. Vampires can use their DT rating instead of their willpower for path rolls. <br /> <br /> -DT requires a working relationship with one or more demons. Should the relationship break down, the character's DT becomes useless. With the right knowledge, the vampire can still pay the difference in XP to recover DT paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T05:21:29-07:00","id":1514682,"title":"","content":"Also I try to balance the paths a bit. There's no such thing as NPC-only magic in my games so things should be adjusted accordingly. <br /> <br /> Lure of Flames is straight up fire, a bane for vampires. Vampires can only resist it with specific magic like Fortitude. <br /> Fires of the inferno is balefire, corrupt fire, not a bane for vampires. Any powers that resist fire or toxin can be used to resist balefire, but also vampires and ghouls can use their stamina. The damage is aggravated for healing purposes. Mortals and Werewolves cannot soak balefire with their stamina, unless they have resist toxin or something like that. Difficulties to avoid fear-frenzies are reduced by 1 for vampires. <br /> <br /> Balefire doesn't spread into natural fires. <br /> Balefire is radioactive. Exposure to the fire's glow, victims of the spell, or the caster of the spell can cause sickness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T05:37:52-07:00","id":1514685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513813-dark-thaumaturgy-is-actually-pretty-cool?p=1514682#post1514682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Balefire is radioactive.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does a vampire recover from getting irradiated? They don't suffer most medical problems from radiation poisoning, but set off alarm bells if they walk around ionizing everything they touch (detection of Orphan Sources is taken very seriously). I don't think it would reset after sleep, so they just.. go into torpor for a few hundred years?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T05:48:09-07:00","id":1514687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513813-dark-thaumaturgy-is-actually-pretty-cool?p=1514685#post1514685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a vampire recover from getting irradiated? They don't suffer most medical problems from radiation poisoning, but set off alarm bells if they walk around ionizing everything they touch (detection of Orphan Sources is taken very seriously). I don't think it would reset after sleep, so they just.. go into torpor for a few hundred years?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>On the contrary, I would say it heals after sleep or healing. Remember that Vampire healing is less cell recovery and more restoration of how things were; if you ripped the tattoo off a vampire it would return. If you filled the leech with plutonium he'd certainly find a way to excrete it. The exceptional case being perhaps the poor sod who was poisoned before the embrace, that might stick to him. In the case of balefire, the radiation source is explicitly magical, so it's fair game to say the radiation just stops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T06:10:30-07:00","id":1514689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513813-dark-thaumaturgy-is-actually-pretty-cool?p=1514687#post1514687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that Vampire healing is less cell recovery and more restoration of how things were; if you ripped the tattoo off a vampire it would return.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, the 'magic stasis' is actually what I perceived to be a problem. With active cell renewal there is at least a chance to get rid of irradiated material, but if you reset everything the lingering ionizing radiation just gets new targets- although I guess you could just not over-complicate things like I do and say balefire doesn't have neutron radiation, lol.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T08:20:14-07:00","id":1514703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513813-dark-thaumaturgy-is-actually-pretty-cool?p=1514662#post1514662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think in general thaumaturgy was supposed to have flashy and attractive powers that really make others envious and thus it's wielders paranoid. DT being MORE flashy in it's application feels a little wasted, and also like something that only noobs would go for while professional sorcerer types would be quite happy with what they got. Like if you have a relatively safe environment and a path towards mastery of Lure of Flames then Fires of the Inferno seems like an extravagance. Rules wise, FoI is strictly more powerful than LoF and if you were to offer a neonate in a bad spot a choice they'd very probably pick FoI but it's more of a masquerade risk and at 5th level in either path everything should die just the same and you probably shouldn't be over-invested in causing death. Similar arguments could be found in corruption VS defiler.<br /> <br /> Personally, I imagine Tremere have the entire infernal library already converted into vanilla thaumaturgy, they just don't teach it because it'll unnecessarily harm their reputation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Blood magic: secrets of Thaumaturgy comments that the Tremere consider the DT paths to be simply lost paths some Demon got its talons and ultimately a lazy dead end since the knowledge is rote learnt rather than a deeper understanding of the principles of magic. I don't think they have automatically have all the paths and rituals but they're probably quite confident they could replicate them if needs be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T13:05:29-07:00","id":1514742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513813-dark-thaumaturgy-is-actually-pretty-cool?p=1514689#post1514689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, the 'magic stasis' is actually what I perceived to be a problem. With active cell renewal there is at least a chance to get rid of irradiated material, but if you reset everything the lingering ionizing radiation just gets new targets- although I guess you could just not over-complicate things like I do and say balefire doesn't have neutron radiation, lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could also treat it like vampirism treats a tattoo: the vampire rejects the foreign material and forces it out.<br /> <br /> It's magic, so there's no reason this wouldn't include free roaming particles of foreign energy. Considering this works against almost Any unwanted tranformations, such as mage curses, unlesss said transformation is specifically hardened to itself restrict vampire healing(which natural radiation is not).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}